&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Growth organization drives Stripe&#39;s self-serve growth engine: from a user&#39;s first interaction with Stripe through onboarding, activation, and expansion across our products. Growth focuses on building the systems and surfaces that help any user find, understand, and adopt the right set of Stripe products, regardless of how or where they start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Growth, the onboarding program is how new and existing users get to their first successful use of Stripe as quickly and completely as possible. A cohesive onboarding experience is critical to Stripe&#39;s ability to convert prospects, activate new products, and compete against increasingly sophisticated alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Onboarding spans several interconnected surfaces:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acquisition and intent capture — first-touch experiences that match prospects to the right products and entry points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account setup and activation — guided flows that get users live with the right integration shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-product discovery — contextual surfaces that help new and existing users adopt additional products over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These surfaces are deeply interdependent, span dozens of cross-functional teams, and directly shape Stripe&#39;s new user activation and product attach rates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are seeking a product-focused Technical Program Manager to drive Stripe&#39;s onboarding programs. This is a high-impact role at the intersection of growth strategy, product management, and cross-organizational program ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In this role, you will own one of the most strategically consequential programs in Growth, driving the direction, health, and outcomes of Stripe&#39;s onboarding experience end-to-end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will set the program strategy in partnership with Growth leadership, holding organizations accountable to the success of the program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-org decisions across DRIs in Growth, Dashboard, Docs, Marketing, and product teams actively resolving the hard, ambiguous integration and ownership questions that fall between team boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and shape product and engineering roadmaps bringing a program-level perspective to team planning cycles, and advocating for cross-cutting investments that no single team will prioritize on their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical program management experience with demonstrated success in driving complex cross organizational programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and ability to understand enterprise customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to communicate with precision and credibility across engineering, product, and executive audiences, translating complex technical trade-offs into strategic decisions, and driving alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead and align cross-functional teams — driving decisions, resolving conflict, and building consensus across organizations with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successful program delivery in complex technical environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in product management or product operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;CSQ427R9&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Program Manager for Scaled User Programs (SUP) in the AMER region is responsible for driving growth in customer training engagement at scale. This role designs and executes structured, repeatable programs that effectively reach broad audiences and convert initial awareness into active participation in learning initiatives. Serving as a key entry point into customer education, the Program Manager partners closely with Sales and Customer Enablement (CEA) teams to deliver consistent, scalable solutions that support customer adoption, improve training outcomes, and contribute to overall account health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Regional Strategic Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and own the AMER Scaled User Programs strategy, ensuring alignment with regional business unit priorities and learner growth targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary regional point of contact, evaluating and prioritizing initiatives to balance global requests with AMER-specific needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular executive-level reporting (e.g., SBAR, MBR) to communicate program performance, risks, and learner funnel insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Operational Excellence &amp;amp; Scalability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational rigor by auditing and optimizing program infrastructure (e.g., Airtable, Docebo, dashboards), ensuring reliability through system-based access and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable, repeatable program frameworks that replace one-off efforts and can be consistently leveraged by regional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear visibility into program demand and capacity through structured tracking of projects, priorities, and stakeholder requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Cross-Functional Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales and Customer Enablement teams to deliver structured learning programs that support customer adoption and growth within priority accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the AMER representative in global forums, advocating for regional needs and ensuring alignment between global strategy and local execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Management: Demonstrated experience managing high-volume, top-of-funnel enablement programs that drive engagement at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Excellence: Proficiency with tools such as Airtable, Docebo, or similar LMS/database platforms, with a strong emphasis on building stable, system-driven processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Management: Ability to navigate complex stakeholder environments, including managing competing priorities and confidently addressing out-of-scope requests to maintain focus on regional objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Planning: Experience developing regional roadmaps that translate broader organizational goals into clear, actionable initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What &quot;Great&quot; Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A successful candidate in this role demonstrates strong ownership of the AMER learner funnel, proactively driving performance rather than simply executing assigned tasks. They serve as a reliable and scalable partner to the Sales organization, enabling consistent impact across a broad customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual operates with a high level of transparency, maintaining clear and structured documentation to track progress, priorities, and outcomes. They also ensure that regional technical infrastructure is robust, scalable, and resilient, with systems designed for continuity and independence from individual contributors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2729&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Databricks is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. The pay range(s) for this role is listed below and represents the expected base salary range for non-commissionable roles or on-target earnings for commissionable roles.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, relevant certifications and training, and specific work location. Based on the factors above, Databricks anticipated utilizing the full width of the range. The total compensation package for this position may also include eligibility for annual performance bonus, equity, and the benefits listed above. For more information regarding which range your location is in visit our page &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/sites/default/files/2024-08/us-pay-zone-mapping.pdf&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$143,700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$197,550 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 2 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$129,300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$177,750 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 3 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$122,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$167,950 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 4 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$158,050 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
